# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository and, crucially, in the
# working tree too.
#
# Without this, a checkout on Windows with core.autocrlf=true rewrites every
# text file with CRLF. Rust and Markdown do not care. Shell scripts do: bash
# reads `check() {\r` and reports a syntax error on a line that looks
# perfectly correct, which is a genuinely baffling ten minutes. The same
# files then ship inside the .deb and run on the appliance.
#
# `eol=lf` is deliberate rather than `text=auto`: this project's scripts are
# executed from WSL and from Linux, never from cmd.exe, so there is nothing
# that wants CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary formats, kept out of newline conversion entirely.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.deb binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
